ed-application": "similarity-checking"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2024, 12, 6]], "date-time": "2024-12-06T13:15:41Z", "timestamp": 1733490941000}, "score": 26.178268, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://neobiota.pensoft.net/article/129679/"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2024, 12, 6]]}, "references-count": 96, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.3897/neobiota.96.129679", "ISSN": ["1314-2488", "1619-0033"], "issn-type": [{"value": "1314-2488", "type": "electronic"}, {"value": "1619-0033", "type": "print"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[2024, 12, 6]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2022, 3, 30]], "date-time": "2022-03-30T03:40:33Z", "timestamp": 1648611633923}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "American Library Association", "issue": "11", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "short-container-title": ["Choice Reviews Online"], "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2008, 7, 1]]}, "DOI": "10.5860/choice.45-6282", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2013, 1, 24]], "date-time": "2013-01-24T08:27:05Z", "timestamp": 1359016025000}, "page": "45-6282-45-6282", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Rules to break and laws to follow: how your business can beat the crisis of short-termism"], "prefix": "10.5860", "volume": "45", "member": "3932", "container-title": ["Choice Reviews Online"], "language": "en", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2016, 8, 11]], "date-time": "2016-08-11T19:13:54Z", "timestamp": 1470942834000}, "score": 24.473885, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "http://choicereviews.org/review/10.5860/CHOICE.45-6282"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2008, 7, 1]]}, "references-count": 0, "journal-issue": {"issue": "11", "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2008, 7, 1]]}}, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.5860/choice.45-6282", "ISSN": ["0009-4978", "1523-8253"], "issn-type": [{"value": "0009-4978", "type": "print"}, {"value": "1523-8253", "type": "electronic"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[2008, 7, 1]]}}, {"institution": [{"name": "National Bureau of Economic Research", "acronym": ["NBER"], "place": ["Cambridge, MA"]}], "indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 9, 12]], "date-time": "2026-09-12T00:18:57Z", "timestamp": 1789172337060, "version": "build-2803163510"}, "publisher-location": "Cambridge, MA", "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "National Bureau of Economic Research", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "DOI": "10.3386/w13714", "type": "report", "created": {"date-parts": [[2007, 12, 28]], "date-time": "2007-12-28T14:18:41Z", "timestamp": 1198851521000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 4, "title": ["Do Professional Currency Managers Beat the Benchmark?"], "prefix": "10.3386", "author": [{"given": "Momtchil", "family": "Pojarliev", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Richard", "family": "Levich", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "1960", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2007, 12]]}, "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 9, 12]], "date-time": "2026-09-12T00:01:51Z", "timestamp": 1789171311000}, "score": 23.934423, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "http://www.nber.org/papers/w13714.pdf"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2007, 12]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.3386/w13714", "published": {"date-parts": [[2007, 12]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2024, 5, 12]], "date-time": "2024-05-12T20:09:47Z", "timestamp": 1715544587532}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Cornell University Press", "isbn-type": [{"value": "9781501755644", "type": "print"}, {"value": "9781501755668", "type": "electronic"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2021, 6, 15]]}, "abstract": "<p>This chapter explicates the functions of rules in simulation. It elaborates on its two central functions in any classroom simulation: the rules tell students what they are allowed to do from class to class, and they tell students what they need to do in order to win the simulation. The chapter argues that simulations do not have to feature wars, but they do need competition and victory conditions. Competition and victory give purpose; they also drive student motivation. Ultimately, the chapter looks at the three examples, <italic>Greenwich Village</italic>, <italic>Galileo</italic>, <italic>Stages of Power</italic> \u2014 none of them featuring simulated armed conflict \u2014 and investigates how they use rules to inform and induce student activities. It then examines <italic>Great Power Rivalries</italic>, which does the same thing, but uses different rules for different students.</p>", "DOI": "10.7591/cornell/9781501755644.003.0004", "type": "book-chapter", "created": {"date-parts": [[2022, 1, 20]], "date-time": "2022-01-20T14:35:12Z", "timestamp": 1642689312000}, "page": "56-70", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Rules"], "prefix": "10.7591", "author": [{"given": "Michael A.", "family": "Barnhart", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "4434", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2022, 1, 20]]}, "container-title": ["Can You Beat Churchill?"], "original-title": ["Rules"], "language": "en", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2022, 1, 20]], "date-time": "2022-01-20T14:35:13Z", "timestamp": 1642689313000}, "score": 23.67179, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://cornell.universitypressscholarship.com/view/10.7591/cornell/9781501755644.001.0001/upso-9781501755644-chapter-004"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2021, 6, 15]]}, "ISBN": ["9781501755644", "9781501755668"], "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.7591/cornell/9781501755644.003.0004", "published": {"date-parts": [[2021, 6, 15]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2022, 8, 3]], "date-time": "2022-08-03T01:12:20Z", "timestamp": 1659489140447}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Oxford University Press", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2011, 2, 15]]}, "DOI": "10.1093/acprof:oso/9780195384055.003.0007", "type": "book-chapter", "created": {"date-parts": [[2011, 5, 11]], "date-time": "2011-05-11T14:18:13Z", "timestamp": 1305123493000}, "page": "160-193", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Who Rules the Beat The Battle Over Managerial Rights"], "prefix": "10.1093", "author": [{"given": "Joshua", "family": "Page", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "286", "container-title": ["The Toughest Beat"], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2022, 8, 3]], "date-time": "2022-08-03T00:36:54Z", "timestamp": 1659487014000}, "score": 23.586163, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://academic.oup.com/book/11009/chapter/159338346"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2011, 2, 15]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.1093/acprof:oso/9780195384055.003.0007", "published": {"date-parts": [[2011, 2, 15]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 8, 11]], "date-time": "2026-08-11T12:32:43Z", "timestamp": 1786451563197, "version": "build-2736575974"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2007]]}, "group-title": "SSRN", "reference-count": 20, "publisher": "Elsevier BV", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "abstract": "<jats:p>We investigate an index of returns on professionally managed currency funds and a subset of returns from 34 individual currency fund managers. Over the period 1990-2006, excess returns earned by currency fund managers have averaged 25 basis points per month. We examine the relationship of these returns to four factors representing returns based on carry trading, trend-following, value trading and currency volatility. These four factors explain a substantial portion of the variability in index returns in the entire period and in sub-periods. We perform similar regressions for the 34 individual funds, and find many funds where returns are significantly related to these four factors. Our approach impacts the definition of alpha returns from currency speculation, modifying it from the excess return earned by the fund, to only that portion of the excess returns not explained by the four factors. While the impact on measured alpha is substantial, we find that some currency fund managers continued to generate alpha returns in the most recent sample period.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.2139/ssrn.1077687", "type": "posted-content", "created": {"date-parts": [[2011, 12, 28]], "date-time": "2011-12-28T12:28:47Z", "timestamp": 1325075327000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Do Professional Currency Managers Beat the Benchmark?"], "prefix": "10.2139", "author": [{"given": "Momtchil", "family": "Pojarliev", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Richard M.", "family": "Levich", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "78", "reference": [{"key": "ref1", "article-title": "The Beta Continuum: Classic Beta, Bespoke Beta, Alternative Beta, Fundamental Beta, Cheap Beta, and Active Beta", "author": "M Anson", "year": "2007", "journal-title": "Journal of Portfolio Management"}, {"key": "ref2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "first-page": "435", "DOI": "10.1086/296139", "article-title": "The 'Speculative Efficiency' Hypothesis", "author": "J F Bilson", "year": "1981", "journal-title": "Journal of Business"}, {"key": "ref3", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "first-page": "52", "DOI": "10.3905/jai.2005.608032", "article-title": "Currency Management Through the Ages", "author": "J Binny", "year": "2005", "journal-title": "Journal of Alternative Investments"}, {"key": "ref4", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1016/s1573-4404(85)02006-8", "article